<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oghuz Turks</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oghuz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Oghuz Turks were a confederation of Turkic tribes who lived on the steppes north of the Caspian and Aral seas. In the eleventh century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qiniq">Qiniq</a> clan of the Oghuz, built the Seljuk Empire and opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> to Turkic settlement. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, was traditionally a chieftain of the Kayı clan of the Oghuz.</p></div>
